---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import registry from '../generated/registry.json';
import coverage from '../generated/coverage.json';
import parameters from '../generated/parameters.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const counts = registry.counts as Record<string, number>;
const unverified = parameters.reduce((n: number, p: { unverified_count: number }) => n + p.unverified_count, 0);
const totalParams = parameters.reduce(
  (n: number, p: { parameters: unknown[] }) => n + p.parameters.length,
  0,
);
const normalized = coverage.totals.normalized;
const expected = coverage.cells.length;
---

<Base
  title="Vermont School Budgets — public, sorted, and yours to try out"
  description="Every Vermont supervisory union's budgets in one clear, sourced form, plus a tool to try out what merging or closing schools would do to your town's spending and home tax rate."
>
  <h1>Vermont school budgets, in the open</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Every Vermont supervisory union has its budgets here, put in one clear form with every number tied back to where it came from.
    There is also a tool that lets you try out what merging or closing schools would do to your town's school spending and home tax rate, with every step of the math shown and linked to the law.
  </p>

  <div class="notice blocking">
    <strong>What this site can and cannot tell you today</strong>
    <p>
      The master list of who exists is complete: {counts['su']} supervisory unions, {counts['ud']} unified districts, {counts['school']} schools, and {counts['town']} towns, pulled from the Agency of Education's public data feed with every raw response saved.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong style="display:inline">No budget documents have been collected yet</strong>, {normalized} of {expected} district-years. 
       The <a href={`${base}/admin/coverage/`}>what-we-have page</a> shows exactly which are missing, and it is public on purpose, so the gaps are easy to see.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong style="display:inline">No legal number has been checked yet</strong>, {unverified} of {totalParams}. 
      Until a person reads a pupil weight or yield straight from the
      current law, the engine won't do math with it and returns nothing instead of a good-looking
      guess. You will see it stop, with the reason, anywhere a number would otherwise show up.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Why it is built this way</h2>

  <h3>Every number can be traced</h3>
  <p>
    Every number on this site has to come from a public source you can check. We store the raw
    budget documents exactly as they were released, never edited, each with a record of where it
    came from, when, who got it, and a fingerprint of the file. When someone asks where a number
    came from and when it changed, the answer is a link to the exact saved change.
  </p>

  <h3>You can check the math</h3>
  <p>
    The math engine runs in your browser, and its code is open. What it gives back is not just a
    number but a tree of steps: each step shows its inputs, what it did, the result, a
    plain-language note, and the source for every legal number it used. Checking the state's work
    only means something if you can check the checking too.
  </p>

  <h3>We show what's missing, we don't make it up</h3>
  <p>
    A blank in this site's data means one of two specific things, and it always tells you which.
    Either the district did not publish that number — noted with who confirmed it and when — or a
    legal number has not been checked against the current law yet. Neither is ever quietly swapped
    for a guess, and the two are never shown as the same thing.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to start</h2>
  <ul class="grid">
    <li class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0"><a href={`${base}/model/`}>The what-if tool</a></h3>
      <p>Build a merger or closure what-if and see the math step by step.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0"><a href={`${base}/su/`}>Supervisory unions</a></h3>
      <p>{counts['su']} pages: their districts, schools, towns, and the budgets we have.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0"><a href={`${base}/methodology/`}>How it works</a></h3>
      <p>How we store budgets, how the engine works, and every number with its source and whether
        it has been checked.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0"><a href={`${base}/admin/coverage/`}>What we have</a></h3>
      <p>Which budgets we have, which are missing, and how to send one in.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>We stay neutral</h2>
  <p>
    This site is independent. It is not made by, for, or against the Agency of Education, any
    supervisory union, or any advocacy group. It does the math and explains it; it does not score,
    rank, or recommend, and it never spins a result as a "saving." A what-if that costs more is
    shown just as prominently as one that costs less, because which one you are hoping for is not
    this site's business.
  </p>
</Base>
